WEBVTT

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.920
Remove your forces from Yamato immediately,

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:50.140
and the Emperor promises he will be merciful—

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.440
Heed me!

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.110
It is not Yamato {who}that shall rule this land,

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.620
but we, the Uzuurussha!

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:21.830
Ye starving wolves, sink your fangs into Yamato's neck,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.370
and let the name of Gundurua be known to all!{MEME}

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.690
Nothing seems to have changed much, even with a war going on.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.740
I thought it'd be more tense, or something.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:16.660
That just goes to show how much the people of this land trust the Emperor.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:17.950
The Emperor, huh?

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:22.280
<i>The first thing you do when war breaks out is stockpile provisions,</i>

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.460
<i>but even that doesn't seem to be happening.</i>

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:30.360
What is it?

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:31.310
You have been summoned.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.120
We have come for you.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:34.620
Okay.

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:39.850
Okay, I'll head back to Hakuroukaku.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.060
Well, let's go then.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:55.350
My apologies for calling you again like this.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:58.870
So what do you want, Your Highness?

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:04.340
So young, yet so forgetful!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.250
My name is Mito. Mito.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.690
Listen...

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:10.220
Here, Haku-sama.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:12.250
Thanks.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.880
How does it taste?

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.440
It's good.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:18.510
Wait, that's not...

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.200
Explain what's goi—

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.940
Please, partake at your leisure.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.020
Thanks.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:28.550
There is plenty more, if you wish.

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:30.010
I appreciate it.

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.200
Wait, that's not...

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.270
Your Highness, what's the deal?

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.410
Why are you so interested in me?

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:38.280
Look...

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:40.400
Please, Mito is fine.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.910
Won't you indulge me that when we're here, at least?

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:50.880
Now then, you wished to know what I was after?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:57.050
I told you before: simply a person to talk with.

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.600
Then it doesn't have to be me, does it?

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.590
You've got the Eight Pillar Generals

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.520
like Oshutoru or Mikazuchi...

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.560
Any of them would be happy to talk to you.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:09.350
Fine servants though they may be,

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:12.810
that itself is the reason I'm unable to converse with them like so.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:17.570
In that sense, you are ideal.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:21.980
You know neither Yamato nor the Emperor.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:24.270
You can speak to me as an equal.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.580
Won't you please call me Mito?

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.580
Fine, old man.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.460
How contrary you are!

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.720
Wait, aren't we in the middle of a war?

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:44.570
Is it really okay for us to be chatting here?

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.190
Of course. I don't mind.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:47.830
You should mind!

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:51.420
I will not interfere trivial matters such as this.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.290
"trival matters"?

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.480
It's a war, right?

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.280
Yamato's history is anything but brief.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:01.590
We are certainly no strangers to matters like these.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.370
And I have men I trust.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:07.870
Let us begin our strategy {conference}meeting.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.650
Seems not everybody's here yet.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.200
Generals Oozen and Soyankekuru

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.750
have sent messengers saying they cannot leave their lands.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:18.770
The Eight Pillar Generals

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:24.800
should never leave the Emperor's side when Yamato is in danger.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.070
Don't you agree, General Munechika?

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.140
General Woshisu, please begin.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:34.150
The Uzuurussha have crossed the river that marks the border and invaded Yamato.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:36.920
They've seized Maruruha,

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:40.120
and are currently sending troops over to our side.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:43.600
Hmph. So they're not satisfied
with just Maruruha?

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:47.660
Given their numbers, they must
be planning something further.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:51.440
Those barbarians should learn their place.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.520
Don't you agree, General Tokifusa?

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.290
Uzuurussha, eh?

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.950
They've raided the border here and there,

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:00.920
but an invasion on this scale is a first.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:05.470
Before, they were little more than small tribes.

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:09.240
But now, someone has
unified them into a nation.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:10.310
His name is...

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:12.430
Gundurua?

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.390
He's an excellent warrior

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:19.190
who united over a hundred tribes in a very short period of time.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.910
An excellent warrior?

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:27.530
He's nothing but an ignorant rube if he thinks he can attack Yamato.

00:07:27.530 --> 00:07:29.200
Don't you agree, General Raikou?

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.770
Is he a clown as well as their chieftain?

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:34.000
He's certainly making me laugh.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.440
How unlike you, General Raikou.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:40.340
Underestimate him and he may well catch you off guard.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:43.390
I never expected a lecture from you.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.900
So I fell victim to arrogance?

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:48.890
I shall heed this as a lesson.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:57.020
The Uzuurussha were brought together under Gundurua's banner.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:01.230
It would be prudent not to think of them as the mere barbarians we've faced prior.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:03.840
Bring together as many barbarians as you want,

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:05.740
{a barbarian is a barbarian.}they're still barbarians.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:08.190
They've no hope against Yamato.

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.120
Don't you agree, General Woshisu?

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:10.120
Now,

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.620
let us appoint the punitive force against these barbarians.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.500
So what are the Eight Pillar Generals, anyway?

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:20.750
Why do you ask?

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:24.280
Well, I can kind of understand the General of the Left and

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:25.680
General of the Right, but...

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:29.350
What do the Eight Pillar Generals usually do?

00:08:29.350 --> 00:08:32.320
Well, perhaps this is a good time.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.140
Let me tell you.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:38.020
The Eight Pillar Generals are the cornerstones of Yamato,

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:41.020
each of whom I found and appointed personally.

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:49.780
Woshisu, Raikou, and Dekoponpo
rule the lands of Yamato in my stead.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.780
Oozen is the Ouro of Kujuuri.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.790
Soyankekuru is the Ouro of Shahhoro.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:59.440
Tokifusa is the Ouro of Izuruha.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:05.050
Their families have served me as Ouros of these lands for generations.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:10.800
The guardian of the capital is the ultimate shield, Munechika.

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:18.090
And Vurai, the ultimate spear, crushes the enemies of Yamato.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.280
I found them all myself.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:28.360
You trust them, huh?

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.570
Oh, can I ask something?

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.310
What is it?

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:34.490
Why'd you choose a guy like Dekoponpo?

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.580
It's more fun with at least one person like him around, no?

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:39.580
Seriously?

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.530
I jest.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:45.840
His father was a very loyal man.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:47.960
I'm repaying that debt.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:49.870
In other words, it's just because of his dad?

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.660
Yes, if I'm to be perfectly honest.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:55.470
Oh, come on...

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:00.100
By the way, how old are you?

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:03.720
I'm afraid I don't remember.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.950
General Vurai shall be the vanguard,

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:10.830
together with General Raikou.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:11.990
I accept.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.210
Behind them will be General Munechika.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:14.990
Understood.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:17.370
Behind her, General Tokifusa.

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:18.240
Good.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:22.320
They shall comprise the punitive force against the Uzuurussha.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:25.180
I shall provide support from within the capital,

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:27.140
so perform to the best of your abilities.

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.250
Additionally,

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:31.090
General Oozen and General Soyankekuru have sent word

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:37.140
that they will send their daughters in their stead.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:42.140
Both Royal Generals shall remain here.

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:43.390
Fine.

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.400
No objections.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:47.280
The force departs in five days.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:49.580
Fellow generals, make preparations for war.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:50.590
Wait!

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:52.720
General Dekoponpo?

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.160
Is there something you wish to say?

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.480
Don't act like you don't know!

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.280
My name wasn't called!

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.980
You're the weakest of the Eight Pillar Generals. What nonsense are you spouting?

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:04.670
Your forces couldn't even serve as shields.

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:07.040
Wh-Wh-What? How dare you!

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:12.850
Well, perhaps we could have you join the next battle after?

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:14.050
Don't be absurd!

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:18.030
Without me, who will show the world our Emperor's glory!?

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:18.810
Be silent.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:19.810
Yes, sir...

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:33.390
I won't forget this!

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:41.930
Shall we prepare our departure, then?

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:43.480
Oh yes, one last matter.

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:46.390
I heard something about the Uzuurussha that concerned me.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.080
And that is?

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:52.450
It seems they're using the people they've captured as hostages by putting them

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:53.970
at the front of their ranks.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.570
Such a barbarous tactic.{:^^^^^)}

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:00.770
Citizens of Yamato from Maruruha, then?

00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:02.290
Likely so.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:05.230
We must keep consideration of their rescue in mind.

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:06.730
Unnecessary.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:11.450
The warriors of Yamato are never defeated.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.990
Thus, any who are defeated are not warriors of Yamato.

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.740
There are no prisoners.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:52.610
I heard the Eight Pillar Generals are about to leave!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:56.740
General Vurai and General Raikou are leading the way.

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:58.940
With those two leading, there's nothing to worry about.

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:02.190
I don't know what the deal is with these Uzuurussha guys,

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:04.350
but this war will be over before you know it!

00:13:13.700 --> 00:13:15.000
So in the end,

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.760
you're not going to war?

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:20.890
Guarding the capital is my duty as Royal General.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:24.760
Subduing foreign enemies is the 
responsibility of the other Pillar Generals.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:27.510
You have that stuff all split up, huh?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.930
But the others are going to grab the glory.

00:13:31.800 --> 00:13:33.020
Indeed.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:35.970
It's unfortunate that I cannot fight for my Emperor,

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:37.560
but that is merely a personal matter.

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:40.380
No matter who gets the glory,

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.030
so long as it helps Yamato, that is most important.

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:44.820
Is that how it works?

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.380
There's no need to worry.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:50.290
General Raikou and General Vurai are at the vanguard this time.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:52.040
Are they strong?

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:55.520
General Raikou's tactics are precise beyond compare.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:59.670
You could search the four seas and never find a strategist his equal.

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:04.680
And this Vurai guy?

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:13.330
I know none so loyal to the Emperor as he.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:19.940
So long as he fights for the Emperor, General Vurai will never be defeated.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.320
You've sure got a high opinion of him.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.040
We have much in common.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:03.830
Vurai-sama!

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:05.160
There's trouble!

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:07.780
Speak!

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:13.040
Woshisu-sama has asked that everyone assemble at once.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:22.540
"Swift and decisive" should be the ideal of the soldier.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:27.050
An inspired decision, Dekoponpo-sama.

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.750
In war, glory goes to he who takes the initiative.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:34.310
I'm not just all talk, like they are.

00:15:34.310 --> 00:15:36.790
You are right, of course!

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:42.670
Your name will be heard all 
across the land after this war!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.840
That's right.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:51.950
General Dekoponpo left without authorization?

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:55.180
I did not expect him to act so rashly.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:58.410
Like feeding a hungry oruke.

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:02.980
General Vurai, where are you going?

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:06.050
I'm departing early.

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:09.750
But even if you leave at once,

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:11.720
you won't catch up to General Dekoponpo.

00:16:11.720 --> 00:16:13.720
That is true.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:16.730
The only one who can leave at once is Munechika, then?

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:20.470
Unfortunately not. General Munechika's forces are primarily infantry.

00:16:20.470 --> 00:16:21.760
They will be unable to catch him.

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:23.860
Then what do we do?

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:28.110
Can I leave this to you, Royal Generals?

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:29.290
Yes.

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.370
Are you mad?

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:38.190
Their forces are primarily cavalry.

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:42.960
Only their forces can catch up to General Dekoponpo.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:49.550
If that mountain of flesh died on the road, 
I would barely shed a tear.

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:52.430
However, Yamato cannot be allowed to suffer repeated defeats.

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:56.640
You've been given the honor of the vanguard. Do not squander it.

00:16:57.020 --> 00:16:58.220
Understood.

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:04.950
Oshutoru...

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:06.400
Yes?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:10.410
I trust you haven't forgotten the Emperor's words?

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:18.910
Of course not.

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:36.430
Sorry to call you at this hour.

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.990
No, it's fine.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:41.630
You're going off to war, too?

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:42.230
Yes.

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:44.090
Oshutoru-sama,

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:45.440
all is ready.

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:52.670
Wait, that outfit...

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.450
You're going off to war too, Nekone?

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.270
Of course.

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:05.640
Here, Oshutoru-sama...

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:14.800
Do I just fill the cup?

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:15.720
Please.

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:16.700
Right.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:43.360
You're supposed to say something now.

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:45.120
Huh? I am?

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:50.260
"I pray for your luck in battle and a long life," perhaps.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:55.140
I pray for your luck in battle and a long life.

00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:57.640
Say it like you mean it!

00:18:58.060 --> 00:19:00.220
Yeah, but...

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:04.030
Do you not fully grasp the meaning of "war"?

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.410
You never change.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:32.080
I'll be leaving, then.

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:50.940
Kiuru...

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:13.090
Ruru-yan.

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:15.440
Atui-sama...

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:19.090
We're doin' this for the sake of our houses, you understand?

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:20.920
Yes.

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:09.810
Father...

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:12.080
Entua?

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:14.990
You're the leader of a thousand men.

00:22:14.990 --> 00:22:18.340
You don't need to watch a supply train leave.

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:23.840
If those supplies don't arrive, 
there's no hope for our comrades.

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:25.970
This is as important a mission as any.

00:22:27.580 --> 00:22:28.910
Oh, I see...

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:32.600
How was your first mission?

00:22:33.050 --> 00:22:34.890
It was nothing!

00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:37.610
There is no need to fear the soldiers of Yamato!

00:22:39.300 --> 00:22:40.610
How brave.

00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:46.240
I am the daughter of the famous Zeguni, Leader of a Thousand!

00:22:46.830 --> 00:22:47.920
Entua...

00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:50.000
Leader of a Thousand!

00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:51.980
The Ouro is calling you.

00:22:51.980 --> 00:22:53.000
Understood.

00:22:53.770 --> 00:22:57.000
Entua, don't waste your life.

00:22:57.000 --> 00:22:58.070
Right!

00:22:58.070 --> 00:23:01.010
I promise not to bring shame on you!

00:23:08.250 --> 00:23:12.950
<i>Starvation and poverty forge us stronger than the soft soldiers of Yamato,</i>

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:17.270
<i>with their full bellies and warm clothes.</i>

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:19.070
<i>But...</i>

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:26.750
<i>"Thou must not awaken a sleeping Akuruturuka," huh?</i>
